<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SMG Holdings 13-month attrib shr in profit.</title>
<headline>SMG Holdings 13-month attrib shr in profit.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>13 months ended March 31 vs year ended February 29</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		3.14	  vs 17.00</p>
<p>    - attrib		  3.14 profit vs 26.80 loss</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 1.00	  vs nil</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   5.95 profit vs 4.44 loss</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   2.11 profit vs 2.93 loss</p>
<p>    Tax			 1.08	  vs 1.60</p>
<p>    Finance costs	   1.22	  vs 0.21</p>
<p>    Turnover		  4.86	  vs 22.04</p>
<p>Exceptional items</p>
<p>- profit on sale of subsidiary</p>
<p>				  nil	   vs 0.62</p>
<p>    Goodwill written off  nil	   vs 7.87</p>
<p>    Share of associates'  4.92	  vs 0.10</p>
<p>Div payable September 4</p>
<p>on register August 20</p>
<p>Full name: SMG Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The share of associates' income relates to SMG purchase of a 73.65 percent stake in New Republic Bank Ltd with effect from March 1, 1996.</p>
<p>Directors said the acqusitions made by sMG, previously a cash shell, was in line with its objective to investmetn in financial services, property and allied businesses.</p>
<p>They said the existing investments provide for substantial growth off a relatively low base. As a result the group expects improved results in the new financial year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
